  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nHigh temperatures on Friday will be slightly warmer near sea level\nto around 5 degrees warmer for the mountains. High temperatures on\nFriday will be around 80 near the coast with the valleys and \ninland coastal areas mostly in the lower to mid 80s.\n\nHigh pressure aloft will weaken and onshore flow strengthen for\nSaturday into early next week which will spread cooling inland.\nHigh temperatures on Saturday for the coast and valleys will cool\n5 to 10 degrees with high temperatures mostly in the 70s. High\ntemperatures on Sunday will cool another 5 degrees or so with high\ntemperatures for the coast and valleys mostly in the upper 60s to\nmid 70s.\n\nA low pressure system moving quickly inland through southern\nCalifornia around Sunday could bring some precipitation for Sunday\ninto Sunday night. A more substantial storm with heavier\nprecipitation is possible for next Tuesday and Wednesday. For next\nTuesday and Wednesday, the chance for 1 inch or more of rainfall \nis 55 to 65 percent for the coast to the mountains. The chance for\n2 inches or more of rainfall ranges from around 25 to 35 percent \nnear the coast to 45 to 55 percent for the San Bernardino County \nmountains. The chance for 5 inches or more of rainfall is around 5\nto 10 percent for the San Bernardino County mountains.",
